{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>עבשו</b> — It has no parallel. Rabbi Marinos said: the scattered grains of wheat and barley that were sown, which are beneath their threshing sledges, have rotted. The meaning is [like] the dust; and thus he would interpret [it], or [as related to] אגרוף [fist], with the alef added." "<b>נהרסו ממגורות</b> — Hired places for grain, like storehouses, as in על דגן ותירוש יתגוררו. And the word is unusual, due to the addition of two mems."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אין לו חבר' (it has no parallel) refers to the rarity of this verb form in Scripture. The subject of 'the meaning is the dust' is uncertain; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:47.081234877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}